"""Phase 2.1 conversation batch B: longer natural multi-turn chats with corrections, clarifications and changes of mind."""
from gen21_common import *

B = Bank("general_conversation", "c21b")
d = B.d

d("multi_clarify", "I need a gift for my dad.", "Happy to help. What's he into, and what's your rough budget? Even a hint like \"fishing\" or \"he loves gadgets\" helps.", "He's 62, retired, likes woodworking. Maybe 60 bucks?", "For a woodworker at that budget: a good marking gauge or a set of sharp chisel-sharpening stones, a quality apron, or a book on joinery such as 'The Complete Illustrated Guide to Joinery' by Gary Rogowski. If he already has most tools, a nice finishing oil and a handful of exotic wood offcuts make a fun, personal gift.", "he already has a ton of tools. the offcuts idea is nice", "Then lean into it: a small box of offcuts in different species, such as walnut, cherry, maple and padauk, with a handwritten note suggesting he make something with them. Add a tin of finishing wax or oil and you're comfortably under 60.")
d("multi_correction", "How many legs does a spider have?", "Eight.", "Insects have eight too, right?", "No, insects have six. Spiders aren't insects; they're arachnids, along with scorpions and ticks, and arachnids have eight legs.", "huh. so what about a centipede", "Centipedes aren't insects either; they're myriapods. They have many legs, at least 15 pairs, and one pair per body segment. Despite the name, the number varies by species and is never exactly 100.")
d("multi_advice", "How do I tell my boss I'm overloaded?", "Pick a calm moment and bring specifics instead of a general complaint. List your current tasks and deadlines, say what you cannot realistically finish, and ask which priorities to drop or move. Framing it as \"I want to do these well\" sounds like commitment, not complaint.", "She tends to just say 'we're all busy'.", "Then make it harder to wave away: send her a short written list ahead of the meeting and ask a decision question, such as \"Of A, B and C, which should I defer to hit the Friday deadline?\" That forces a choice. If she still dismisses it, note the date and what you raised, so there is a record.")
d("multi_recipe", "Quick dinner for two, vegetarian, 20 minutes?", "Chickpea and spinach curry: fry garlic, ginger and a spoon of curry powder, add a can of chickpeas, a can of chopped tomatoes and a handful of spinach, simmer for 10 minutes. Serve with rice or bread.", "no tomatoes, I'm allergic", "Good to know. Use coconut milk instead of tomatoes: after frying the spices, add a can of coconut milk and the chickpeas, simmer for 10 minutes, then wilt in the spinach and add lemon juice at the end for brightness.", "can I swap the spinach for kale", "Yes. Kale is tougher, so strip the stems, chop it small and give it 5 to 7 minutes of simmering instead of just wilting it.")
d("multi_tech_help", "My Excel formula =SUM(A1:A5) shows 0 but the cells have numbers", "The numbers are probably stored as text. Look for a small green triangle in the cells, or left-aligned numbers. Select the cells and use the warning icon to convert to number, or use Data > Text to Columns > Finish.", "they're left aligned yes", "That confirms it. After converting, SUM should work. If the numbers came from a pasted source, trailing spaces can also cause it; =VALUE(TRIM(A1)) converts a single cell.")
d("multi_trip", "We're going to Iceland in March. Worth it?", "Yes, if you want snow-covered scenery and a chance at the northern lights, which peak in winter. Daylight is limited, around 11 to 12 hours by late March, and weather changes quickly, so road conditions can disrupt plans.", "will we see the aurora for sure?", "No guarantee. It depends on solar activity, clear skies and darkness. Plan several nights, check the aurora forecast and cloud cover each evening, and go away from town lights. Many visitors who stay four or five nights see it, but some don't.")
d("multi_shopping", "Which is better for a student, a laptop or a tablet?", "For most students, a laptop: it handles writing, spreadsheets, research and coding comfortably. A tablet works well if your coursework is mostly reading and handwritten notes.", "I do a lot of handwritten notes in my art degree", "Then a tablet with a stylus becomes a strong option for sketching and note-taking. If you also need to write long essays, add a keyboard case or consider a convertible laptop with a pen. Check if your software, such as Adobe or Procreate, runs on the device.")
d("multi_correction_self", "What's the boiling point of water at the top of Everest?", "About 71 degrees Celsius, because air pressure is roughly a third of that at sea level.", "Are you sure? I thought it was lower", "Reasonable doubt. Estimates vary with the day's pressure, but they usually land around 68 to 71 C. Pressure at the summit is about 33 kPa, which corresponds to a boiling point of about 71 C, so my figure is at the top of that range and 70 would be a fair rounded answer.")
d("multi_confused", "I don't understand fractions", "That's fine, let's start small. A fraction is a part of a whole. If a pizza is cut into 4 equal slices and you eat 1, you ate 1/4. The bottom number is how many equal parts, the top is how many you have.", "ok so what's 2/4", "2/4 means two of four slices. That's half the pizza, so 2/4 = 1/2. When you divide the top and bottom by the same number, here 2, you get an equal fraction in simpler form.", "ohh. so 3/6 is also half?", "Exactly. 3 and 6 can both be divided by 3, giving 1/2. Whenever the top is exactly half the bottom, the fraction equals one half.")
d("multi_planning", "Help me plan a birthday party for 8 kids aged 7", "Keep it simple: 90 to 120 minutes is ideal at that age. A typical flow is arrival and free play for 15 minutes, a main activity or two such as a scavenger hunt or a craft, food and cake, then goodie bags. Do you have a place and a theme in mind?", "backyard, dinosaur theme", "Dinosaur dig: bury plastic dinosaurs or bones in a sandbox and give each child a brush and cup. Add a fossil craft with air-dry clay and leaf or shell prints, and a dino stomp game like musical statues. Menu ideas: 'dino nuggets', fruit 'volcano' platter and green jelly. Have a plan B for rain, such as a garage or a rented tent.")
d("multi_language", "How do you say 'where is the bathroom' in Spanish?", "\"¿Dónde está el baño?\"", "and politely?", "\"Disculpe, ¿me podría decir dónde está el baño?\" which means \"Excuse me, could you tell me where the bathroom is?\"", "how do I say 'thank you very much'", "\"Muchas gracias.\" For something warmer, \"Muchísimas gracias\" or \"Se lo agradezco mucho\" in a formal setting.")
d("multi_decision", "Should I take a job with higher pay but a 90 minute commute?", "It's worth putting a number on the commute. 90 minutes each way is 15 hours a week, so compare the pay difference per extra hour. Also consider remote days, whether you can work on a train, and the effect on sleep and time with family. People tend to underestimate how much commuting wears them down.", "pay is 15% more, 2 remote days", "With two remote days, you'd commute three days, about 9 hours a week, if the 15% is substantial in your case that could be fair. Check what 15% is in actual money after tax, and subtract commuting costs. If it's under what you'd pay to get that time back, or if you'd be exhausted, I'd lean no. Is the new role also better for your career?")
d("multi_confusion_term", "What's the difference between weather and climate?", "Weather is what's happening in the atmosphere now or over days: today's rain or temperature. Climate is the long-term pattern, usually averaged over 30 years or more.", "so one cold winter doesn't disprove global warming?", "Right. A single cold winter is weather, a short-term local event. Climate trends are measured over decades and across the globe, and global averages have risen over the past century even though individual winters can be cold.")
d("multi_budget", "I make about 3000 a month after tax. How should I budget?", "A common starting point is the 50/30/20 rule: roughly 50% needs (1,500), 30% wants (900), 20% savings and debt repayment (600). Adjust to your situation: if rent is high, needs may be 60%.", "my rent is 1400 alone", "Then needs will exceed 50% once food, transport and bills are added, perhaps 65 to 70%. A realistic version could be 70% needs (2,100), 10% wants (300), 20% savings (600), or trim savings to 15% for a while. Track your spending for a month, then see where the real room is.")
d("multi_story", "Write me a two-line story about a lighthouse keeper", "The lighthouse keeper had watched ships for forty years and never once been waved at. Tonight, a tiny boat flashed its lantern back, and he laughed until he cried.", "make it sadder", "The keeper lit the lamp every night for a ship that never came home. Tonight, one lantern blinked back from the dark water, and then went out.")
d("multi_style_change", "Summarise the plot of Romeo and Juliet", "Two teenagers from feuding families in Verona fall in love and secretly marry. After Romeo kills Juliet's cousin Tybalt, he's banished. Juliet fakes her death with a potion to escape a forced marriage, but Romeo doesn't get the message, believes she's dead and kills himself. Juliet wakes, finds him dead and takes her own life. Their deaths finally end the families' feud.", "now explain it as if you're texting a friend", "ok so two teens from rival families fall for each other and secretly marry. then romeo gets in a fight and kills her cousin so he gets exiled. juliet fakes her death to avoid marrying someone else, but romeo never gets the memo, thinks she's dead and ends himself. she wakes up, sees him, does the same. the families finally stop fighting. rough.")
d("multi_misc_question", "What's the best way to learn touch typing?", "Use a structured trainer such as Keybr, Typing.com or TypingClub, practise 15 to 20 minutes daily, keep your fingers on the home row, and look at the screen, not the keys. Accuracy first; speed follows.", "how long until I'm fast", "Most people reach a comfortable 40 wpm within a few weeks of daily practice, and 60 or more in a couple of months. It varies, and progress comes in plateaus.")
d("multi_apology", "You gave me a wrong answer earlier about the capital of Canada", "I'm sorry for that. The capital of Canada is Ottawa, in Ontario, not Toronto or Montreal. If I gave you something else earlier, please disregard it. Is there anything depending on that answer I can help correct?")
d("multi_tease", "tell me something I probably don't know", "Honey found in Egyptian tombs is said to have remained edible after thousands of years, thanks to its low moisture and natural acidity, though you'd want to check any such claim with an archaeologist before tasting it.", "ok I did know that. another", "Fair enough. Octopuses have three hearts: two pump blood through the gills and one through the rest of the body, and the main heart stops while they swim, which is partly why they prefer crawling.")
d("multi_roommate", "Is it rude to ask a guest to take off their shoes?", "Not at all, it's common in many countries. Make it easy by saying it warmly, such as \"We keep shoes off inside, there are slippers by the door.\" A basket and a few spare slippers help guests feel comfortable.", "what if they have foot problems", "Then relax the rule. Say, \"No worries, whatever's comfortable,\" and if they need supportive shoes, offer a clean pair of indoor shoes or put down a mat. Guests with medical needs come before house rules.")
d("multi_math_everyday", "Is it cheaper to buy a 500g pack for 3.40 or a 750g pack for 4.95?", "Compare the price per 100 g. The 500 g pack is 3.40 / 5 = 0.68 per 100 g. The 750 g pack is 4.95 / 7.5 = 0.66 per 100 g. The larger pack is slightly cheaper, by 2 cents per 100 g.", "worth it if I won't use all of it?", "Only if you'd use it before it spoils. If a quarter of the large pack gets thrown out, you'd pay about 4.95 for roughly 562 g of usable food, which is 0.88 per 100 g, worse than the small pack.")
d("multi_vague_start", "hey", "Hi! What can I help with?", "idk im bored", "Then let's find something. Do you feel like a quick game, like 20 questions or a riddle, learning a random fact, planning something fun for later, or just chatting?", "riddle", "Here's one: I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with wind. What am I?", "echo?", "Yes, an echo. Want a harder one?")
d("multi_overwhelmed", "i have 4 deadlines this week and i'm freezing up", "That freeze is common when everything feels equally urgent. Let's break it down. What are the four tasks, and when is each due? Even a quick list is enough.", "essay fri, lab report thu, quiz wed, presentation mon", "Order by due date: presentation (Mon), quiz (Wed), lab report (Thu), essay (Fri). Today, take the earliest and do one 45-minute block on it. Quiz prep can be short, reviews in 20-minute chunks, and the essay can get an outline early so you aren't starting cold Thursday night. Which of these feels hardest to start?")
d("multi_tone_check", "Did my message sound rude? 'Send me the file ASAP, I can't keep waiting.'", "It's a bit sharp. \"I can't keep waiting\" can read as blame. You could say, \"Could you send the file today if possible? I need it to move forward.\"", "ok. and what if they've been late three times", "Then be direct but factual: \"I've been waiting on this file since Monday and it's now blocking my work. Could you send it by 3 p.m. today? If something is holding it up, tell me so I can plan.\" You've named the impact without accusing them.")
d("multi_diet", "Is intermittent fasting healthy?", "For many healthy adults it can be a way to cut calories and has some evidence for weight loss, but it isn't clearly better than ordinary calorie control. It is not suitable for everyone, such as people who are pregnant, have diabetes on certain medicines, or have a history of eating disorders.", "I'm on blood pressure medication", "Then check with your doctor first. Changes in eating patterns can affect how some blood-pressure medicines work, and fasting can change hydration and blood pressure itself. Your doctor knows your medication and can tell you if it's safe.")
d("multi_dispute", "I think my friend is wrong. Napoleon was super short, right?", "He wasn't unusually short. He was about 5 feet 6 or 5 feet 7 inches in modern units, around average or slightly above for French men of his time. The myth came partly from confusion between French and English inches and British cartoons.", "so my friend is right?", "If your friend said he wasn't short, yes. Napoleon was about average height for his era.")
d("multi_naming", "I need a name for my bakery", "A few directions: warm and simple (\"Golden Crumb\"), local (\"Corner Oven\"), playful (\"Rise & Shine\"), or personal (your name or a grandparent's). Do you have a vibe, a town or a speciality?", "sourdough, small town, cosy", "For cosy sourdough: \"The Little Loaf\", \"Hearth & Starter\", \"Mother Dough Bakehouse\" or \"Slow Rise\". Say them aloud and check that the web address and social handles are free before you commit.")
d("multi_fix_text", "Make this sound more professional: 'hey guys, just checking if u got my email'", "\"Hello team, I'm following up on my earlier email. Could you let me know if you received it?\"", "shorter", "\"Hi all, did you receive my earlier email?\"")
d("multi_history", "Why did the Roman Empire fall?", "Historians cite many causes: political instability and civil wars, economic strain and inflation, military pressure from groups such as the Goths and Huns, and the split of the empire into east and west. The western empire's end is usually dated to 476, when Romulus Augustulus was deposed.", "did the east fall too?", "Not then. The eastern half, the Byzantine Empire, continued for nearly another thousand years until Constantinople fell to the Ottomans in 1453.")
d("multi_user_correct", "What's 15% of 80?", "12.", "I think it's 14", "Let me check: 10% of 80 is 8 and 5% is 4, so 15% is 8 + 4 = 12. If you got 14, you may have added 6 instead of 4 for the 5% part. 12 is right.")
d("multi_schedule", "Can you help me make a study schedule? Exams start in 3 weeks and I have 4 subjects", "Yes. Two quick things: how many hours a day can you study, and which subject is the weakest? That decides how to split time.", "3 hours on weekdays, 5 on weekends. maths is weakest", "That's about 25 hours a week. Roughly: maths 9 hours, the other three subjects 5 hours each, and one hour weekly for mixed review. Week 1: learn and fix gaps; week 2: practice questions; week 3: past papers under time and light review. Alternate subjects within a day so it doesn't get stale.")
d("multi_cynical", "Why is everything so expensive now?", "A mix of things: inflation after supply disruptions and energy price spikes, higher interest rates raising borrowing costs, wages and rents rising, and in some places housing shortages. The mix varies by country and by item.", "Wages haven't kept up though", "In many places, that's true for a stretch of recent years: prices rose faster than average pay, so real purchasing power fell for many households, though it differs by country, job and age group. If you tell me where you are, I can be more specific.")
d("multi_quiz", "Quiz me on world capitals", "Sure. Question 1: What is the capital of Brazil?", "Rio de Janeiro", "Close, but Brasília is the capital. Rio was the capital until 1960. Question 2: What is the capital of Turkey?", "Ankara", "Correct. Question 3: What is the capital of Nigeria?", "Abuja", "Right, it replaced Lagos in 1991. Score so far: 2 out of 3.")
d("multi_apology_slow", "this is taking forever", "Sorry about the wait. What are you trying to do? If I know the task, I can suggest a quicker route.", "converting a pdf to word", "For a quick conversion, open the PDF in Word directly (File > Open); Word will convert it. For scanned PDFs, you'd need OCR. A tiny PDF should take seconds; if it's stuck, close and retry, or try a free online converter only for non-sensitive documents.")
d("multi_gift_return", "Is it OK to regift something?", "Generally yes, if it's new, unopened and the original giver won't meet the new recipient. Check there are no personal tags or notes, and make sure it suits the person.", "my aunt gave me a candle I don't like", "Then a candle is an easy regift. Just check that it isn't engraved or scented in a way that suits you, and choose a recipient who doesn't know your aunt.")
d("multi_work_email", "Help me write to my landlord about a leaking tap", "Here's a draft:\n\n\"Hello [Name], the kitchen tap has been leaking since [date]. Could you arrange a repair? I'm available [days/times]. Please let me know when someone can come. Thank you, [Your name].\"", "he's been ignoring me for 2 weeks", "Make the tone firmer and add a record: \"Hello [Name], I first reported the leaking kitchen tap on [date] and haven't had a reply. The leak is continuing and may cause damage. Please confirm by [date] when a repair will be arranged. I'm keeping a record of my messages.\" Send it in writing, and check your tenancy rules for repair deadlines.")
d("multi_biology", "Do humans really have five senses?", "That's the traditional list (sight, hearing, smell, taste, touch), but scientists recognise more: balance, body position sense, temperature, pain and internal sensing such as hunger.", "what's proprioception then", "It's the sense of where your body parts are without looking. It's why you can touch your nose with your eyes closed. It relies on receptors in muscles and joints.")
d("multi_book_chat", "I can't get into 'Moby Dick'. should I stop?", "You don't have to finish it. It's famously digressive, and many readers skim the whaling chapters. If you enjoy the story, try reading only the narrative chapters, or use an audiobook. If nothing grabs you, put it down and try something shorter.", "its the whale encyclopedia parts", "Those are the chapters people skip most. They're skippable without losing the plot, though they carry the book's themes. Read the opening, then chapters with Ahab and the chase, and return to the cetology if you feel like it.")
d("multi_soft_pushback", "Can you just tell me what to do? I hate making choices", "I can give a recommendation if you tell me the options. I may not know your whole situation, so I'll point out my reasoning and you can overrule me. What are you choosing between?", "pizza or sushi for dinner", "Pizza, if you're tired and want comfort food; sushi if you want something lighter. Since you hate choosing: go with pizza. It's easy to share and reheat tomorrow.")
d("multi_dumb_question", "stupid question but how do you know if an avocado is ripe", "Not stupid. Gently press it in your palm: it should give slightly without feeling mushy. Peel back the little stem cap; green underneath means ripe, brown means overripe. Dark skin colour helps for Hass avocados but isn't reliable alone.", "and if it's hard?", "Leave it on the counter for a few days, or put it in a paper bag with a banana to speed it up.")
d("multi_boundaries_friend", "my friend keeps cancelling last minute", "That's frustrating. Is it a pattern, or has it been recent? And have you told them it bothers you?", "pattern, and no i haven't said anything", "Then it's worth a calm, specific message: \"I've noticed the last few plans fell through. I miss seeing you, but I'd rather plan fewer things that happen. Is something going on?\" It states your feelings without accusing, and it gives them room to explain.")
d("multi_weather_chat", "Do you think it'll rain tomorrow?", "I can't see weather forecasts or your location, so I can't say. A weather app or your national forecast service will be much better. If you tell me the forecast, I can help you decide what to wear or plan.")
d("multi_music_taste", "I like Radiohead and Bon Iver. What else?", "You'd likely enjoy Sufjan Stevens, Fleet Foxes, The National and James Blake. For more electronic textures with emotional vocals, try Jon Hopkins or Sigur Ros.", "something less sad", "Try Beach House for dreamy calm, Father John Misty for sarcasm and warmth, and Real Estate for easy, breezy guitar. Another option is Caribou for brighter electronic pop.")
d("multi_estimate_help", "How long would it take to walk 10 km?", "At a typical walking pace of 5 km/h, about two hours. A brisk pace of 6 km/h takes around 1 hour 40 minutes.", "and 15 km, with breaks?", "About 3 hours of walking at 5 km/h, plus breaks. If you stop for 10 minutes each hour, expect roughly 3.5 hours in total.")
d("multi_meaning", "What does 'bite the bullet' mean?", "It means to face something unpleasant and get on with it. It may come from soldiers biting a bullet during surgery without anaesthetic, although the origin is uncertain.", "use it in a sentence", "\"I hate going to the dentist, but I decided to bite the bullet and book the appointment.\"")
d("multi_moral_dilemma", "Is lying ever okay?", "Many ethical views accept some lies, such as lying to protect someone from harm, while others, like Kant's, hold that lying is always wrong. Most people judge by harm, intent and context.", "what would you do", "I try to be honest, so I wouldn't lie to you, but I'd choose kind and tactful honesty over blunt harm. For a human facing a case where telling the truth gets someone hurt, I'd say protecting them can outweigh strict honesty, though it's a judgement call.")
d("multi_silly", "can penguins fly", "Not through the air. Their wings have turned into flippers that help them 'fly' through water, where they're fast and graceful.", "so a penguin is a fish", "No, still a bird. It has feathers, lays eggs and breathes air. The flipper-like wings just evolved for swimming.")
d("multi_cleaning", "How often should I wash my bed sheets?", "About once a week is a common recommendation, or every two weeks if you want to stretch it. Wash more often if you sweat, have pets in bed or have allergies.", "and the pillow?", "Pillowcases weekly with the sheets. The pillows themselves can be machine-washed every three to six months if the label allows, and replaced roughly every one to two years.")
d("multi_nerd_chat", "What's the difference between a virus and bacteria?", "Bacteria are single-celled living organisms that can reproduce on their own, and many are harmless or helpful. Viruses are much smaller, aren't cells, and need a host cell to replicate.", "that's why antibiotics don't work on colds?", "Yes. Antibiotics target bacterial processes, like cell walls, and viruses don't have these. Colds are caused by viruses, so antibiotics do nothing against them and just contribute to resistance.")
d("multi_resolution", "I want to read more this year. How?", "Tie it to a habit: 15 pages before bed, or reading at lunch. Keep a book where you'd normally grab your phone, and choose books you actually want to read, not ones you think you should.", "I can never finish books", "Give yourself permission to quit. Try the 50-page rule: if it hasn't hooked you by page 50, stop. Shorter books and audiobooks can restart the habit, and a book club helps with accountability.")
d("multi_data_privacy_chat", "Is it safe to use public wifi for banking?", "It's risky. Prefer your mobile data. If you must use public wifi, make sure the banking site or app uses HTTPS, turn on two-factor authentication, and use a reputable VPN as an added layer, but avoid it for anything sensitive when you can.", "ok and what about hotel wifi", "Treat it as public wifi: many people share it, and a password doesn't mean it's secure. Use your phone's hotspot for banking.")
d("multi_directions", "how do I get better at giving presentations", "Know your first minute by heart, use few words per slide, and rehearse out loud at least twice. Slow your pace more than feels natural, and look at people, not the slides.", "I get shaky hands", "That's common. Hold a clicker or a card to steady them, plant your feet, and breathe out longer than in before you begin. Nobody sees the shake as much as you feel it.")
E_ = None

if __name__ == "__main__":
    save("conv21_b", B.records())
